  "uncertain": [
   "Macross pack-suffix punctuation is inconsistent in the glossary and was kept as given: VF-25F/VF-25G 'F/TP','B/TP'; VF-25S 'F.TP','B.TP'; RVF-25 'F/SP' but 'B.SP'; YF-29 'F.SP','B.SP'. Suggest normalising the glossary to one separator (all short forms here use '/').",
   "VF-27γ Lucifer: glossary English says 'YF-27γ Lucifer Super Pack [Fighter/Battroid]'; the unit is the VF-27γ, so en uses 'VF-27γ Lucifer Super Pack [Fighter]' / '[Battroid]' (glossary entry looks wrong).",
   "超銀河グレンラガン / 超銀河ダイグレン: kept the glossary/current 'Super Galaxy' (dialogue and battle voice use it too); the official English is 'Super Galaxy'. Short forms 'SG GurrenLagann' / 'TT GurrenLagann' drop a space to fit 15.",
   "Short forms coined to fit 15: 'Ptolemaios2 Kai', 'Quatre-V.-Dix', 'Heavyarms Cust.', 'Deathscythe H', 'Stand. Tortoise', 'Hvy Ship Vajra', 'Hvy Mob. Vajra', 'Titan Grav Src', 'Exelio Grav Src', 'Quarter Ship' (fortress-ship mode), 'Combined Type' (space monster).",
   "ＶＢ－６ケーニッヒモンスターＳ short 'Koenig Monster' drops the S (assumed the shuttle-mode short name; no other Koenig variant in this brief).",
   "ケルビム・ヴェルルゼバ short 'Verlzeva' and ケルビム兵 short 'Cherub Soldier' (Cherub = singular of Cherubim)."
  ],
  "notes": "80/80 items. Full names from the glossary or the brief's current; ＦＡ・ユニコーンガンダム uses the glossary's proposed 'FA Unicorn Gundam'. ？？？ = '???', ダミー = 'Dummy'."
